      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"scientific\" arguments relied heavily on the discredited pseudoscience of eugenics and social Darwinism, claiming that white people were biologically superior and that mixing races would lead to the extinction of the white race. Proponents also argued that segregation was essential for social stability, asserting that keeping races separate prevented \"race mixing\" which they falsely believed would destroy white culture and moral character. They frequently cited the \"one-drop rule\" as a biological fact to justify strict separation, claiming that any African ancestry automatically disqualified someone from white society. These arguments were constructed to maintain white supremacy by framing inequality as a natural law rather than a social construct.",
